{"name":"Screaming Bell Metal","hex":"#c16f45","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"screaming","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Loud, sharp, and piercing to the ear.","Obvious; distinct."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A scream."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/screaming"},{"term":"bell","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A percussive instrument made of metal or other hard material, typically but not always in the shape of an inverted cup with a flared rim, which resonates when struck.","An instrument that emits a ringing sound, situated on a bicycle's handlebar and used by the cyclist to warn of their presence."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To attach a bell to.","To shape so that it flares out like a bell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bell"},{"term":"metal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Chemical elements or alloys, their ores, and the mines where their ores come from.\n Any of a number of chemical elements in the periodic table that form a metallic bond with other metal atoms; generally shiny, somewhat malleable and hard, often a conductor of heat and electricity.\n\n Any material with similar physical properties as those chemical elements, especially as a combination of several of them, such as an alloy.\n\n An element which was not directly created after the Big Bang but instead formed through nuclear reactions; any element other than hydrogen and helium.\n\n Crushed rock, stones etc. used to make a road.\n\n The ore from which a metal is derived.\n A mine from which ores are taken.","Any of a number of chemical elements in the periodic table that form a metallic bond with other metal atoms; generally shiny, somewhat malleable and hard, often a conductor of heat and electricity."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Characterized by strong drum-beats and distorted guitars. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Having the emotional or social characteristics associated with metal music; brash, bold, frank, unyielding, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/metal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bell metal","blocks":[{"text":"Bell metal or bell bronze is an alloy used for making bells and related instruments, such as cymbals. It is a form of bronze with a higher tin content than most other bronzes, usually in approximately a 4:1 ratio of copper to tin. The higher tin content increases the rigidity of the metal, and increases the resonance. Historically, it was preferred for early cannons. Today, it also has industrial uses, being specified for valve bodies, piston rings, bearings, and bushings."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Malik_E_Maidan.jpg/330px-Malik_E_Maidan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bell_metal","wikidata":"Q1660564"},{"title":"Screaming","blocks":[{"text":"A scream is a loud/hard vocalization in which air is passed through the vocal cords with greater force than in regular or close-distance vocalisation. This can be performed by any creature possessing lungs, including humans."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Baby_yelling.jpg/330px-Baby_yelling.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Screaming","wikidata":"Q1932016"},{"title":"Bell","blocks":[{"text":"A bell is a directly struck idiophone percussion instrument. Most bells have the shape of a hollow cup that—when struck—vibrates in a single strong strike tone, with its sides forming an efficient resonator. The strike may be made by an internal \"clapper\" or \"uvula\", an external hammer, or—in small bells—by a small loose sphere enclosed within the body of the bell."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Parts_of_a_Bell.svg/330px-Parts_of_a_Bell.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bell","wikidata":"Q101401"},{"title":"Metal","blocks":[{"text":"A metal is a material that, when polished or fractured, shows a lustrous appearance, and conducts electricity and heat relatively well. These properties are all associated with having electrons available at the Fermi level, as opposed to nonmetallic materials which do not. Metals are typically ductile and malleable."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Iron_electrolytic_and_1cm3_cube.jpg/330px-Iron_electrolytic_and_1cm3_cube.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metal","wikidata":"Q11426"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Jingyun_bell.jpg/330px-Jingyun_bell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Jingyun_bell.jpg/330px-Jingyun_bell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Jingyun bell, cast in 711, weighing 6,500 kg, originally from the bell tower at the Tang dynasty capital Chang'an","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJingyun_bell.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/The_Scream.jpg/500px-The_Scream.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/The_Scream.jpg/1280px-The_Scream.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/The_Scream.jpg/500px-The_Scream.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Scream, Edvard Munch ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Scream.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/One_World_%21.jpg/500px-One_World_%21.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/One_World_%21.jpg/1280px-One_World_%21.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/One_World_%21.jpg/500px-One_World_%21.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Screaming for good","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOne_World_!.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Anger_during_a_protest_by_David_Shankbone.jpg/500px-Anger_during_a_protest_by_David_Shankbone.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Anger_during_a_protest_by_David_Shankbone.jpg/1280px-Anger_during_a_protest_by_David_Shankbone.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Anger_during_a_protest_by_David_Shankbone.jpg/500px-Anger_during_a_protest_by_David_Shankbone.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A verbal altercation between two people during a protest in New York City.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnger_during_a_protest_by_David_Shankbone.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Scream_It_%288663414194%29.jpg/500px-Scream_It_%288663414194%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Scream_It_%288663414194%29.jpg/1280px-Scream_It_%288663414194%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Scream_It_%288663414194%29.jpg/500px-Scream_It_%288663414194%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&ut